---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Interests" activeTab="interests">
  <div style="animation: fadeIn 0.5s ease-out;">
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-serif); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Interests & Research</h1>
    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      Here is an overview of the key concepts and methods that drive my scientific curiosity and research projects.
    </p>

    <div class="interests-grid">
      <div class="interest-card">
        <div class="interest-icon">🔋</div>
        <h3 class="interest-title">Active Matter</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.925rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">
          Studying collective behavior in out-of-equilibrium systems where individual components consume energy to produce motion (e.g., self-propelled particles). I investigate glassy dynamics and collective phase behavior.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="interest-card">
        <div class="interest-icon">🕸️</div>
        <h3 class="interest-title">Statistical Mechanics</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.925rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">
          Analyzing macroscopic behaviors from microscopic interactions, particularly in disordered systems and glassy transitions. I am fascinated by thermodynamics, entropy-driven transitions, and fluctuations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="interest-card">
        <div class="interest-icon">🎲</div>
        <h3 class="interest-title">Monte Carlo Methods</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.925rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">
          Utilizing stochastic simulations (like Markov Chain Monte Carlo, Metropolis-Hastings) to model many-body systems. I have built simulations for models ranging from the 2D Ising model to dense active liquids.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="interest-card">
        <div class="interest-icon">🔍</div>
        <h3 class="interest-title">Inverse Problems</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.925rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">
          Developing algorithms to reconstruct underlying interaction potentials or forces directly from particle coordinates. This includes Boltzmann Inversion and force inference techniques for coarse-grained modeling.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  @keyframes fadeIn {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
</style>
